From 987032a97b824aa3fbfa1febba7a1ec9016d9e02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:30:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(bridges): stop left click on the desktop opening the root
 menu

labwc's default mousebinds open the root menu on a left press on the desktop. With a touchpad that was easy to trigger by accident, and since releasing over a menu item activates it, a stray tap-and-drag could open or run whatever item the cursor ended up on.

Bind a left press on Desktop to Focus and keep the root menu on a right press, loaded after <default /> since labwc keeps the later of two identical mousebinds. Bump rc.xml to version 5 and merge the template's mouse settings and contexts into existing configs during migration, keeping any the user already has.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
---
